\description{
Uses ClassyFire's batch submission API to obtain
chemical ontology information (kingdom/superclass/class/...) for many
SMILES in one or a few requests, rather than one request per compound
(see \code{\link[=classyfire_lookup]{classyfire_lookup()}}).
}
\details{
ClassyFire's per-compound endpoint (see \code{\link[=classyfire_lookup]{classyfire_lookup()}}) only
accepts one InChIKey per request and is aggressively rate-limited,
making it impractical for more than a few dozen compounds. ClassyFire
also provides a batch submission API
(\href{https://bitbucket.org/wishartlab/classyfire_api/src/master/}{wishartlab/classyfire_api})
\itemize{
\item \verb{POST .../queries.json} with many structures at once, then poll
\verb{GET .../queries/<id>.json} until finished - which this object uses
instead: one submission (or a handful, via \code{n_batches}) covers the whole
input. This batch endpoint takes a \strong{SMILES or InChI} string (not a bare
InChIKey) per compound; each is submitted as an \verb{<value><TAB><value>}
pair so ClassyFire echoes the value back as its \code{identifier}, letting
results be matched back to the original rows by exact equality rather
than relying on ClassyFire's undocumented internal ordering.
}
}
